nr_id":"comfyliterals","ver":"bdddb08ca82d90d75d97b1d437a652e0284a32ac","Node name for S&R":"Int"},"widgets_values":["1440"]},{"id":194,"type":"Note","pos":[-4735.10205078125,-395.59075927734375],"size":[401.0707092285156,194.34469604492188],"flags":{},"order":10,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Image Resize","properties":{},"widgets_values":["The de-lighting serves to remove the lighting from the image.  The larger the texture, the better the final result is.  But if you get it too high, it will simply look bad.  This is the balance that worked for me, but feel free to play with that, and maybe an upscaler, to make things look better.\n\nNOTE - this is best in a unified square.  Feel free to experiment with sizing."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":197,"type":"Note","pos":[-2417.435791015625,1056.5072021484375],"size":[550.2116088867188,237.30972290039062],"flags":{},"order":11,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"WTF IS THIS?!","properties":{},"widgets_values":["This one was the most difficult for me to get right.  \n\nEssentially what it does is take 'camera shots' of the model and spray paints it on.  It rotates to all of the angles, and then put it all together in the end. \n\nOriginally I thought \"More is better\" which is certainly true, but when I went to go do human faces, it looked pretty awful, so I scaled back from the front.  Feel free to play with it.  The format is separated by commas - ex [90,135,180,215,270,0,0,0] is 8 cameras.  Line it up with the other three, and you will have the proper setup.\n\ncamera_azimuths - I don't know wtf an azimuth is, it's just the rotation around the model\n\ncamera_elevations - the height of the camera (in degrees)\n\nview_weights - When things are spraypainted on, it indicates the strength of it.  So, I made some stronger than others so that it didn't have weird overlap.  \n\n"],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":88,"type":"Hy3DSampleMultiView","pos":[-432.04876708984375,310.5974426269531